# Mailer

## Framework semantics

CakePHP ships `Cake\Mailer\Mailer` for composing and sending email. Prefer Mailer classes + config transport over Laravel Mailable/Notification inventions.

## Required behavior

- Put email composition in Mailer classes; keep controllers/commands as thin callers.
- Configure transports in config; secrets in env/`app_local`.
- Prefer after-commit / queued sending when email must not roll back DB work (pair with transactions decision).
- Do not invent `Mailable` / `Mail::` facades.

## Anti-patterns

- Laravel Mailable / Notification APIs
- Sending email inside Entity callbacks without project convention
- Hardcoding SMTP credentials in Mailer classes

## Review checklist

- [ ] Mailer class owns templates/subject
- [ ] Transport config is environment-safe
- [ ] Failure handling is explicit
